      "content": "Although some discomfort from eye strain might indeed lessen with rest and over-the-counter remedies, the presence of a shadow or curtain-like vision isn't a common symptom of eye strain and could signify a more serious issue. It's crucial to not ignore this experience, as it could be indicative of a retinal problem, which can have urgent consequences. If you continue to experience these symptoms, I highly recommend at least a consultation with an eye care professional today. Your vision and health are too important to risk, and while waiting room times can be long, your safety and well-being are paramount. There may be options available for faster evaluation. Waiting for the right moment could mean risking irreversible damage to your eyesight. Splitting the difference by visiting during a less busy time might reduce your waiting period without significantly impacting your schedule.",
